# When a system enforces invariants across multiple coupled (preference)

Standing user preference: When a system enforces invariants across multiple coupled layers, treat all affected layers as a single atomic unit of change — updating one layer must be propagated consistently across all coupled layers.

## Conventions
- When a system enforces invariants across multiple coupled layers, treat all affected layers as a single atomic unit of change — updating one layer must be propagated consistently across all coupled layers.

